STEP 9 -- PERSISTENCE ACROSS A REAL REBOOT OF THE DUT
------------------------------------------------------------
Objective: the configuration survives a real power-on-reset-equivalent reboot and the feature
still works afterwards -- measured on the wire, not read off `show running-config`.
**Nothing is written to startup-config.**  A NAMED boot config is staged and the pointer put
back afterwards, exactly as groups B and C did.

  Re-applied on the DUT, then staged (23:17:2x):
    awplus(config)# router bgp 65001 / bgp router-id 1.1.1.1
                    neighbor 10.0.61.2 remote-as 65002
                    neighbor 10.0.41.2 remote-as 65003
    awplus# copy running-config flash:/ckT43858.cfg          (tools/ckyn.py)
    awplus(config)# boot config-file flash:/ckT43858.cfg     (config mode)
    awplus# show boot
