9. FINDINGS RAISED BY THIS CASE (next free numbers; F-5 and OPEN-5 were the highest in use)
------------------------------------------------------------
  F-6  BGPv4 on this build is NOT service-gated, unlike OSPFv2 and RIP on the same software.
       `service bgp` exists but takes only `evpn`; the bare form is `% Incomplete command.`
       bgpd runs from boot on both an atlnz-licensed x960-56 and a Base-licensed x960-28.
       Consequences: a "service bgp first" script hits a `%` that makes a stop-on-error driver
       abandon the whole BGP configuration; and a BGP reboot-persistence limb leaves NO sticky
       `no service bgp` line, so its teardown diff CAN come back clean.  For platforms/x960.md.
  F-7  `show running-config` renders ` bgp graceful-restart` on a freshly created `router bgp`
       instance while `copy running-config` writes ` no bgp graceful-restart` and the DUT's own
       BGP OPEN advertises no Graceful Restart capability.  Display disagrees with both the
       saved file and the wire.  Cosmetic here; wants a developer's answer on which is intended.
       For platforms/x960.md and FOR THE TEST ENGINEER.
  O-6  🔴 **RETRACTED BY THIS TESTER BEFORE HAND-BACK.**  O-6 was first raised as "the port
       mirror copied zero frames on `direction receive`, a fourth instance of the
       platforms/x960.md 5 defect class".  **It is withdrawn: the mirror worked.**  The 0-byte
       file was an unflushed buffer behind a `kill -INT` that never reached the tcpdump
       process; the same capture, read once the process was really stopped, holds the mirrored
       echo replies and 14 mirrored TCP/179 packets, all timestamped inside the mirror's own
       window.  **Section 5's M1/M2/M3 are unaffected and still stand.**
       What replaces O-6 is a measurement-method caution, which is worth more:
       **a `tcpdump -w` file SIZE read after an unverified kill is not a measurement** --
       confirm the process has exited, or read tcpdump's own `N packets captured` line.
       Section 5's own evidence is built on capture sizes, so this belongs beside it.
       Still true and separately recorded: configuring a port as a mirror destination removes
       it from its access VLAN, and `no mirror interface` does not put it back.
  O-7  (tool) `interface <mirror-destination-port>` emits `% ... is currently configured as a
       mirror-port. Use caution when altering its config`, which cfg.py treats as an error.
       Combined with the asynchronous `entered disabled state` console lines from the following
       `shutdown`, the batch stopped and LEFT THE PORT SHUT.  Candidate for console.ADVISORY --
       but only with a transcript showing the following command took effect, per the rule in
       tools/README.md.
  TECHNIQUE  The DUT's own `tcpdump` at privileged exec is the right instrument for any
       unicast control-plane protocol on this platform (BGP, TCP-based anything), because such
       traffic never reaches a host NIC on another segment and the port mirror cannot be
       trusted.  `tcpdump -i vlan61 -c N -nn -v tcp port 179`, triggered from the PARTNER's
       console so only one driver touches each /dev/uN.  BPF `greater 90` isolates UPDATEs from
       keepalives (the 14-byte Ethernet header counts: a keepalive is an 85-byte frame).

================================================================================
VERDICT: PASS -- BGPv4 proven end to end on hardware across nine counted dataplane legs and
four protocol captures: two eBGP sessions Established to two partners, the prefixes carried in
real BGP-4 UPDATE messages (Version 4 OPEN, ORIGIN IGP, AS_PATH {65002}, NEXT_HOP 10.0.61.2),
forwarding 0/5 -> 5/5 with an unrouted control at 0/5 and the DUT's own address at 5/5 in every
leg, eBGP AD 20 displaced by a static at AD 1 with the EGRESS MOVE attributed on the wire by
ICMP sourced from the other partner, one prefix withdrawn to 0/5 while the second neighbour's
prefix stayed 5/5 in the same capture and the session stayed Established, removal returning
config, FIB (`% Network not in table`) and dataplane to baseline, and persistence across a real
60 s reboot with both sessions up and both prefixes forwarding 12 s after the interfaces came
up.  Teardown diffed CLEAN on all three devices.  Two findings recorded (F-6 the absent BGP
service gate, F-7 the graceful-restart display/save disagreement) and one observation (O-7);
neither finding is a failure of BGPv4.  **O-6, a claimed port-mirror defect, was RETRACTED by
this tester before hand-back after the instrument was re-checked -- the mirror had worked and
the 0-byte capture was an unflushed buffer behind a kill that never landed.  The retraction and
the measurement-method lesson that replaces it are recorded in step 6a and in section 9.**
